div.p:
It is therefore plain that the heirs of King Atahualpa
          and the other kings and lords
          and all the peoples and nations of those kingdoms of Peru
          had the most abundant right to declare war on the Spaniards
          for five causes:
          namely, the cause of defense;
          the cause of coercion or repulsion of evil men;
          the cause of recovery of seized things
          or of compensation for lesions or harms inflicted upon them;
          the cause of vengeance for injuries;
          and finally the cause of necessity,
          in order to acquire or defend peace and liberty, etc.
